custom-inserts-eval.text:
Pt. was seen at our North/South location for an evaluation and impression for custom Left/Right foot orthotics.

Subjective & Clinical Indications:
Pt. presents with severe foot and ankle pain exacerbated during weight-bearing, standing, and walking, which significantly limits daily functional activities and ambulation.
Diagnosis: {Diagnosis: Pes planovalgus / Plantar fasciitis / Metatarsalgia / Heel pain / Heel varus with forefoot supination / Posterior tibial tendon dysfunction}
Shoe Size: {Shoe Size: 5 / 5.5 / 6 / 6.5 / 7 / 7.5 / 8 / 8.5 / 9 / 9.5 / 10 / 10.5 / 11 / 11.5 / 12 / 12.5 / 13 / 13.5 / 14 / 14.5 / 15 / Other}

Symptoms & Functional Limitations: {Symptoms: Severe medial arch pain / Plantar heel pain with first morning steps / Metatarsal head pain and burning / Lateral foot fatigue and instability}
Static Evaluation: Left/Right {Biomechanics: pes planus with medial longitudinal arch collapse / hindfoot valgus / excessive pronation / rigid high arch / forefoot varus / heel varus with forefoot supination}.
Palpation: Tenderness noted along the {Palpation: plantar fascia insertion / medial calcaneal tubercle / metatarsal heads / posterior tibial tendon / navicular}.
Range of Motion & Alignment: Subtalar joint demonstrated {Subtalar: full range of motion / restricted motion / reducibility to neutral}. Forefoot-to-rearfoot relationship was assessed.
Gait Analysis: Left/Right stance phase demonstrated {Gait: excessive late-stance pronation / early heel rise / antalgic gait / poor shock absorption / reduced propulsion}.

Treatment Plan, Impression & Device Specifications:
Impression taken today for custom-molded functional foot orthotics utilizing {Method: 3D optical scan / foam impression casting / plaster slipper cast} with the subtalar joint held in neutral position and midtarsal joint locked.
Fabrication Lab: {Lab: Pacific Labs / Rx Orthotic Lab / Apis / Apex / Dr. Comfort / Langer / Mile High / Anodyne / Feet First}
Shell & Posting: {Shell: Semi-rigid polypropylene / Rigid thermoplastic / Flexible EVA / Carbon composite} with {Posting: intrinsic rearfoot posting / extrinsic rearfoot post / deep heel cup / medial arch reinforcement}.
Design Additions: {Additions: None / Metatarsal pad / Metatarsal bar / Balance bar / Heel cushion / Deep heel cup / Poron mid-layer / First ray cutout}
Top Cover Material: {Top Cover Material: Spenco / Neoprene / Plastazote / Leather / Vinyl / Bamboo / Poron / EVA}
Top Cover Length: {Top Cover Length: Full-length / 3/4 length / Sulcus length}
{+ Parent Present: Parent/caregiver was present during the evaluation and casting process.}

Patient Education & Financial Protocol:
Pt. was advised that these custom foot orthotics are self-pay / non-covered items, and all out-of-pocket costs and payment policies were discussed and agreed upon.
Explained expected timeline for custom fabrication and scheduled delivery appointment for fitting, shoe integration, and break-in instructions.
All questions were answered to the patient's satisfaction.
